#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# correlation

#% text
# `correlation(xs, ys)` gives Pearson's correlation coefficient of two lists of the same length, the covariance divided by both standard deviations. `correlation(m)` gives the matrix of correlations of the columns of `m`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
correlation([1, 2, 3, 4], [2, 4, 5, 9])
#% output
#= (11/130)*130^(1/2)

#% cell
correlation([10, 20, 30], [3, 2, 1])
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
correlation([[1, 2], [2, 3], [4, 4]])
#% output
#= [[1, (3/14)*21^(1/2)], [(3/14)*21^(1/2), 1]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `covariance`, `std_dev`
